# Shown by /lib/partman/init.d/05kubeos-require-network when a machine has no
# network address at all, so the installation is stopped instead of producing a
# node that can never start.
#
# Compiled format, not source format: cdebconf's template_load() matches
# "Description: " and does not understand the "_Description:" spelling.
#
# Loaded by /lib/main-menu.d/92-kubeos-require-network at main-menu startup.

Template: kubeos/require-network
Type: error
Description: No network address on this machine
 KubeOS is a Kubernetes platform, and the node is bound to its own IP
 address when the cluster is created on first boot. A machine with no
 network address would install successfully and then never come up.
 .
 The installer found no IPv4 address, no default route and no nameserver.
 .
 Connect a wired interface, or a wireless card supported by the firmware in
 this image, and then choose "Partition disks" again.
